WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.220
We are here with Joel McHale

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.439
and Danielle Pinnock in the house.

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:05.880
(audience cheers)

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.970
I first met our next
guest a couple years ago

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.070
when he joined my team on The Voice

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.020
and my sister first fell
in love with his voice

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.060
and she was like, "I love
this guy on your team."

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.590
He's an awesome musical talent

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.240
as you heard at the
beginning of this show.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.220
But he's an equally awesome human

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.280
which is what I love most
about people on my team.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.920
He has a new single
called "Close to Love."

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.892
Let's welcome Corey Ward, everybody.

00:00:27.892 --> 00:00:30.071
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:30.961
So, lemme introduce you.

00:00:30.961 --> 00:00:32.930
This is Danielle, this is Joel.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:33.763
- Hello. Hello. What's up?

00:00:33.763 --> 00:00:35.050
- And we've had a bit of
wine, Corey, so there you go.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.660
- [Corey] Yeah, I'm jealous.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.891
- I'm trying to keep
it together. (giggles)

00:00:37.891 --> 00:00:38.850
(Danielle laughs)

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.132
I'm warm all over. Okay.

00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:42.030
I met you in Season 20-

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:42.863
- Yes, ma'am.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:43.830
- of The Voice.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.030
But you had auditioned

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.620
the previous season as well, right?

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.623
- [Corey] I did.

00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:50.340
I, I never planned to do a show like this

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.300
and I never cared for,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.340
but my family's watched
the show for years-

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.173
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:55.500
- and they begged me to do it.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.000
And I was like, "No, I
don't care to do it."

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.110
- I'm glad they pushed you.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:58.943
- [Corey] Yeah, I know.

00:00:58.943 --> 00:01:00.750
But I was like, I, I
don't care to do that.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.640
But they're like, "Listen, do it."

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.200
And I knew when my Mom

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.570
ended up getting diagnosed with cancer,

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.500
and I was like, "You know what?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.620
If I'm ever gonna do something
like this, it's now."

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.040
Because I wanted something my
family could just celebrate

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.240
instead of hang out in that-

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.073
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:17.643
- just sad, darkness kind of thing.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.550
But I was like, here we go.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.160
And then I didn't get chairs on 19,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.650
but came back for Season 20,

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.450
and I knew that I wasn't done.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.180
My Mom ended up having a
small seizure during 19

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.530
and my family couldn't be there.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.330
So I was like, all right,
that's why I didn't get chairs.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.190
And I came back and I
was like, you know what?

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.750
Now my family's with me now I got it.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.360
And you know, I was excited,

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.100
and so glad that you turned for me.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.933
- You know what it is, (audience applauds)

00:01:41.933 --> 00:01:42.859
timing though.

00:01:42.859 --> 00:01:43.763
Like it's,

00:01:43.763 --> 00:01:45.480
even in all of our careers,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.950
there's timing when things happen

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.720
and your whole spirit isn't into it,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.040
emotionally you're somewhere else.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.450
Like, that happens to all of us.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.040
I'm so glad you picked me.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.840
How, how do you, how do you think you'd do

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.460
as a contestant on one of those shows?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.300
I wanna know your style.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.043
- I would, I would get the show canceled.

00:01:59.043 --> 00:02:00.120
(laughter)

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:00.990
Are you kidding me?

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:01.823
- Honest to God,

00:02:01.823 --> 00:02:03.240
I think you being on Blake's team

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.346
would be the best television ever.

00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:07.350
It would be the best television.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.485
- I'd probably sing, "Let's
get Drunk and Screw," but

00:02:09.485 --> 00:02:11.460
(laughter)

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.013
- Which is why you
probably would pick Blake.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.517
It's like coming home.

00:02:16.517 --> 00:02:18.690
So tell us about your new
single, "Close to Love."

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.830
- Yeah. "Close to Love."

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.260
Um, when I write, I really
want it to be relatable.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.280
Again, just connect.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.706
And what it's about is basically

00:02:25.706 --> 00:02:28.804
getting in a relationship
that feels like love

00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:31.177
and being scared to leave
it because you're like,

00:02:31.177 --> 00:02:33.090
"What if I never get this close again?"

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.080
- Ooh. Ooh.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.720
- [Corey] Because so many people get stuck

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.370
and feel like they gotta stay in something

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.320
because they're afraid of like,

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.780
what if this is the best I can get?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.680
- [Kelly] It's a comfort zone.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.000
- Yeah, it's a comfort thing.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.037
And I just wanted to break that and,

00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:48.300
and relate people with that.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.220
Like, I think we've all
been there at some point.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.053
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:51.053 --> 00:02:52.920
And it also kind of, it's
almost like "Already gone,"

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.540
which I've sung on the show.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.650
- God. You sang it better.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.157
It's literally the only
time I've been like,

00:02:57.157 --> 00:02:58.380
"They just sang it better than I did.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.496
That's cool. Fine."

00:02:59.496 --> 00:03:00.329
(audience laughs)

00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:01.162
- That made my life.

00:03:01.162 --> 00:03:03.390
- I'm not, and by the
way, I wasn't kidding.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.223
So it was-

00:03:04.223 --> 00:03:05.056
- [Corey] It means a lot.

00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:06.330
so moving, coming from a,

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.710
the texture of your voice

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.260
and you could feel that
you meant the lyrics, but.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.420
It's almost like the
opposite of "Already Gone."

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.253
- [Corey] Yeah, exactly.

00:03:13.253 --> 00:03:14.086
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:14.086 --> 00:03:16.090
- It's the the the push
and pull of each other.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:16.923
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:16.923 --> 00:03:17.756
- And I love that

00:03:17.756 --> 00:03:19.803
and I connect with you a lot musically

00:03:19.803 --> 00:03:22.110
and, and that's why I
was so blessed to be here

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:23.370
and very grateful for you.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.203
- Oh my gosh

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.920
I can't wait to have you
back singing more music.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.870
- Hey, I'd love to come back
and sing one of my singings.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:28.703
- I love it.

00:03:28.703 --> 00:03:29.536
- Yes, let's do it.

00:03:29.536 --> 00:03:30.369
- [Kelly] It's so, it's so good.

00:03:30.369 --> 00:03:31.650
I love your voice so much.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.492
- [Corey] Thank you.

00:03:32.492 --> 00:03:33.800
You like, make my heart
smile. It's so good.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:34.800
- It really means,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.530
words will never be able to
tell you how grateful I am.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.790
- Well, I love having you on a team.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.623
It's always awesome.

00:03:39.623 --> 00:03:40.530
Like I get, people don't get it.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.060
Like, a lot of us coaches,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.110
John and I talk about this a lot too.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.060
You get re-inspired in
like a different way

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:45.893
working with-

00:03:45.893 --> 00:03:46.726
- [Corey] Yeah.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.140
- these artists because
it's like, well it's true.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.040
Like because people,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.690
I think sometimes we can get jaded.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.720
When you're in any industry
for a certain amount of time,

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.610
you, you start thinking
you've heard everything.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.080
And then you like, you're sitting there

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.670
and you just hear something so magical

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.923
that like hits you.

00:04:00.923 --> 00:04:02.160
And that's beautiful.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.120
That's a gift.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:03.953
- Yeah. Thank you so much.

00:04:03.953 --> 00:04:04.786
- [Kelly] Anyway. I love you.

00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:05.619
You know this. I'm gonna keep gushing.

00:04:05.619 --> 00:04:06.628
Um, thank you so much, Corey.

00:04:06.628 --> 00:04:07.461
- Thank you so much.

00:04:07.461 --> 00:04:09.863
- I can't wait to see you
come back sing some more.

